== (2) Theorem 5(a) lower bound ==
   (i) drift: rho alpha - 1 = gamma - 1 = -c: identity.
   (ii) E Y_i = i j/t' with j = ceil(rho t') <= rho t' + 1, so E Y_i <= rho i + i/t' <= rho i + 1: identity.
   (iii) Hoeffding (1963, Thm 4 -> Thm 2, values in [0,1]): P(mean dev >= x) <= exp(-2 i x^2); x = c/(2 alpha) gives exp(-c^2 i/(2 alpha^2)): matches the note.
   (vii) block end: the note claims 4 * 2^((gamma-1)(t+1)) >= 4 n^(gamma-1) for n in [2^t, 2^(t+1)). With gamma - 1 = -c < 0, n^(gamma-1) is DEcreasing in n,
        so its maximum over the block is at n = 2^t, namely 2^(-ct) > 2^(-c(t+1)). The claimed inequality is FALSE for every n in the block:
        gamma=0.82 t=100: 4*2^((gamma-1)(t+1)) = 1.346898e-05 < 4 n^(gamma-1) at n = 2^t = 1.525879e-05  (ratio 2^(-c) = 0.8827)
        gamma=0.85 t=100: 4*2^((gamma-1)(t+1)) = 1.100159e-04 < 4 n^(gamma-1) at n = 2^t = 1.220703e-04  (ratio 2^(-c) = 0.9013)
        gamma=0.88 t=100: 4*2^((gamma-1)(t+1)) = 8.986208e-04 < 4 n^(gamma-1) at n = 2^t = 9.765625e-04  (ratio 2^(-c) = 0.9202)
        gamma=0.91 t=100: 4*2^((gamma-1)(t+1)) = 7.340021e-03 < 4 n^(gamma-1) at n = 2^t = 7.812500e-03  (ratio 2^(-c) = 0.9395)
        gamma=0.94 t=100: 4*2^((gamma-1)(t+1)) = 5.995401e-02 < 4 n^(gamma-1) at n = 2^t = 6.250000e-02  (ratio 2^(-c) = 0.9593)
        gamma=0.97 t=100: 4*2^((gamma-1)(t+1)) = 4.897101e-01 < 4 n^(gamma-1) at n = 2^t = 5.000000e-01  (ratio 2^(-c) = 0.9794)
        What is needed for M_i n >= 4 n^gamma on the whole block is S_i(w) >= -ct + 2 (n = 2^t is the worst case).
        The margin actually available from the stated K, (c + 0.585) K >= delta_0 + c + 2, is S_(K+l)(w) >= (c+0.585)K - ct - delta_0 >= -ct + c + 2 > -ct + 2:
        the '+c' in the K condition is exactly the slack that repairs the step (or, without it, the weaker M_i n >= 4 * 2^(-c) n^gamma >= 3.5 n^gamma still beats the carry).
   (viii) carry: 4 n^gamma - (3/2)^t >= n^gamma iff (3/2)^t <= 3 n^gamma; with n >= 2^t this holds for EVERY t when gamma >= log_2(3/2) (no t_0 needed).
   (vi) margin algebra: 0.585 K - c t' - delta_0 = (c + 0.585) K - c t - delta_0; the note's target -c(t+1) + 2 needs (c+0.585)K >= delta_0 - c + 2, weaker than the stated condition.
   constants table (3) of the original script recomputed (i_0 = min{i : q^i/(1-q) <= 1/2}, q = exp(-c^2/(2 alpha^2))):
      gamma=0.82 c=0.18 i_0=   891 delta_0=   521.20 K_0=   685 (K needed for -ct+2:    684); with K_0: S_(K+l) + ct >= 2.798 >= 2 + c = 2.180: True; cost 2^(-K_0 E) = 9.42e-207
      gamma=0.85 c=0.15 i_0=  1363 delta_0=   797.30 K_0=  1088 (K needed for -ct+2:   1088); with K_0: S_(K+l) + ct >= 2.335 >= 2 + c = 2.150: True; cost 2^(-K_0 E) = 0.00e+00
      gamma=0.88 c=0.12 i_0=  2286 delta_0=  1337.22 K_0=  1900 (K needed for -ct+2:   1900); with K_0: S_(K+l) + ct >= 2.204 >= 2 + c = 2.120: True; cost 2^(-K_0 E) = 0.00e+00
      gamma=0.91 c=0.09 i_0=  4419 delta_0=  2584.95 K_0=  3833 (K needed for -ct+2:   3833); with K_0: S_(K+l) + ct >= 2.182 >= 2 + c = 2.090: True; cost 2^(-K_0 E) = 0.00e+00
      gamma=0.94 c=0.06 i_0= 11074 delta_0=  6477.87 K_0= 10047 (K needed for -ct+2:  10047); with K_0: S_(K+l) + ct >= 2.064 >= 2 + c = 2.060: True; cost 2^(-K_0 E) = 0.00e+00
