== (3) Theorem 5(c) ==
   (i) uniform drift: alpha/2 - 1 = -0.207519 = -c_0 = -(1 - log_4 3): identity.
   (ii) reduction: S_(K+l)(w) = 0.585 K + S_l(v) > 0.585 K - c_0 t' - delta' = 0.585K - c_0 t' - (c_0+0.585)K + 2 = -c_0 (t' + K) + 2 = -c_0 t + 2 >= -c t + 2 because c >= c_0 and t > 0: correct direction, and the target -ct + 2 is the RIGHT block end (unlike (a)).
   (iii) Hoeffding, independent letters: P(alpha Y_i - i >= delta'/2) = P(Y_i/i - 1/2 >= (c_0 i + delta'/2)/(alpha i)) <= exp(-2 (c_0 i + delta'/2)^2/(alpha^2 i)) <= e^(-2 c_0 delta'/alpha^2) e^(-2 c_0^2 i/alpha^2).
      q = e^(-2 c_0^2/alpha^2) = 0.966296, sum_(i>=1) q^i = q/(1-q) = 28.6700, e^(-2 c_0 delta'/alpha^2) at delta' = 29: 0.008302
      factorised bound at delta' = 29: 0.23802 (<= 1/4: True); exact sum at delta' = 29: 0.00592
      smallest integer delta' with the factorised bound <= 1/4: 29; with the exact sum <= 1/4: 17
      delta' = (c_0 + 0.585) K - 2 >= 29 iff K >= 39.118, i.e. K >= 40 (note: K >= 40: True)
   (iv) endpoint: P(S_(t')(v) >= E S_(t')(v)) = P(Bin(t',1/2) >= t'/2) >= 1/2 EXACTLY for every t' (binomial symmetry), so the CLT is not needed and the good fraction is >= 1 - 1/4 - 1/2 = 1/4 for all t' >= 1:
      min over t' <= 400 of P(Bin(t',1/2) >= t'/2) = 0.500000 (>= 1/2: True)
   (v) multiplicative carry below log_2(3/2): integer check at gamma = 1/2, t = 30 (additive bound useless: (3/2)^30 = 1.92e+05 > n^(1/2) = 2^15 = 32768), words with min_i S_i in [-ct+2, -ct+2.6] = [-13, -12.4]:
      sheet b=+1: 2111/2111 representatives have no dip below n^(1/2) within 30 steps
      sheet b=-1: 2111/2111 representatives have no dip below n^(1/2) within 30 steps
      control, min S_i in [-ct-3, -ct-2] (M_i n <= n^gamma/4), sheet b=+1: 0/306 have no dip (expected 0)
      control, min S_i in [-ct-3, -ct-2] (M_i n <= n^gamma/4), sheet b=-1: 0/306 have no dip (expected 0)
   [time 8.1s]

