== (5) exact DP for W_t(gamma) = #{w in {0,1}^t : o_j alpha - j > (gamma - 1) t, 1 <= j <= t}, gamma = p/100 ==
   exact criterion: o alpha - j > (p/100 - 1) t  <=>  3^(100 o) > 2^E, E = 100 j - (100 - p) t; for E > 0 no tie is possible (alpha irrational),
   E < 0 admits every o >= 0, and E = 0 is an EXACT TIE at o = 0 (1 > 1 is false, so o = 0 is excluded by the strict inequality).
   tie flips: (t, gamma) pairs where j = (100-p) t/100 is an integer and the float threshold admits o = 0 at that j:
