== (6) Lemma 1.4b: theta in (0, theta_1], rho = (1-theta)/alpha in [0.565465, 0.630930), k >= 200, o_0 = ceil(rho k - 2) ==
   (rho - 1/2) k >= 13 for k >= 200: worst (rho_min - 1/2) * 200 = 13.0930 (>= 13: True)
   ratio bound (1 - rho + 2/k)/(rho - 2/k) <= 0.81: worst (rho_min, k=200) = 0.80029 (True); 1/(1-0.81) = 5.2632 <= 5.3 (True)
   p(1-p) >= rho*(1-rho*) = 0.232857 (note: 0.2329; 1/sqrt(2 pi 0.232858) = 0.82673, note uses 0.827: safe True)
   (rho/(1-rho))^2 < (rho*/(1-rho*))^2 = 2.92243  (note says <= 2.92: False -- the supremum is 2.9224, so the rounded constant should read 2.93)
   product of the note's rounded constants 5.3 * 2.92 * 0.827 = 12.7987; product of the true suprema (1/0.19) * 2.92243 * 0.82673 = 12.7161; both <= 12.8: True
   representatives: 2^k > X/2 so a class mod 2^k meets [1, X] in at most 2 integers: factor 2.  k >= log_2 X - 1 >= 0.995 log_2 X iff log_2 X >= 200: given.
   final constant: 2 * 12.8 / sqrt(0.995) = 25.6642 <= 27: True
   numerical verification: R(k, theta) = sum_(o >= o_0) C(k, o) * k^(1/2) / 2^(k h(rho)) on theta in {1e-9, 1e-6, 1e-4, 1e-3, 0.005, 0.01, ..., 0.10, theta_1} and every k in [200, 3000] (QUICK: step 25):
      max R over the grid = 5.8187 at (k, theta) = (2971, 0.10375937481971098)  (<= 12.8: True; <= 13.5 for the two-representative form 2 S <= 27 2^(k h) k^(-1/2): True)
      max R per theta: 1e-09:5.799  1e-06:5.800  1e-04:5.798  0.001:5.778  0.005:5.743  0.01:5.698  0.02:5.607  0.03:5.538  0.04:5.495  0.05:5.466  0.06:5.462  0.07:5.490  0.08:5.542  0.09:5.625  0.1:5.759  0.1038:5.819
   [time 58.5s]

== (7) section 1.6b ==
   (i) concavity: h(rho) <= h* + h'(rho*)(rho - rho*) with rho - rho* = -theta/alpha and h'(rho*) = log_2((1-rho*)/rho*) = -0.773584 = -alpha lambda* (-0.773584): so h(rho) <= h* + lambda* theta.
      max over theta in (0, theta_1] (10^4 grid) of h(rho) - h* - lambda* theta = -1.328e-10 (must be <= 0: True)
   (ii) (R'): 1.5 gives N(X) <= k + k N(X^(1-theta)) + #F_b(X, theta) with (E) <= k <= L = log_2 X; 1.4b bounds #F_b for theta <= theta_1 and X >= 2^200 uniformly in theta: (R') follows.
   (iii) X^(1 - theta_X) = X 2^(-theta_X L) = X 2^(-c_1 log_2 L) = X L^(-c_1); X^(h(rho)) <= X^(h* + lambda* theta_X) = X^(h*) L^(lambda* c_1): identities.
   (iv) lambda* c_1 - 1/2 = a* + eta lambda*/h* = a* + 0.51379 eta; need <= a - eta = a* + 3 eta (eta = (a-a*)/4): true since 0.51379 <= 3. Checked on a grid of a:
      a=0.0138 eta=0.000003 c_1=1.052684  lambda* c_1 - 1/2 = 0.013791  a - eta = 0.013797  ok: True
      a=0.0140 eta=0.000053 c_1=1.052736  lambda* c_1 - 1/2 = 0.013816  a - eta = 0.013947  ok: True
      a=0.0200 eta=0.001553 c_1=1.054315  lambda* c_1 - 1/2 = 0.014587  a - eta = 0.018447  ok: True
      a=0.0500 eta=0.009053 c_1=1.062210  lambda* c_1 - 1/2 = 0.018441  a - eta = 0.040947  ok: True
      a=0.1000 eta=0.021553 c_1=1.075369  lambda* c_1 - 1/2 = 0.024863  a - eta = 0.078447  ok: True
      a=0.5000 eta=0.121553 c_1=1.180637  lambda* c_1 - 1/2 = 0.076242  a - eta = 0.378447  ok: True
      a=1.0000 eta=0.246553 c_1=1.312222  lambda* c_1 - 1/2 = 0.140466  a - eta = 0.753447  ok: True
   (v) the step uses only log_2 Y <= L for Y = X L^(-c_1) (no monotonicity of Y -> Y^(h*) (log_2 Y)^a is needed; it is monotone anyway: d/dY[h* ln Y + a ln log_2 Y] = h*/Y + a/(Y ln Y) > 0 for Y > 1);
       2 L^(-eta) + L^(-a) <= 1 and 27 <= K close the induction; K = max(X_3, 27) covers the base 2 <= X < X_3 since N(X) <= X.
   (vi) well-foundedness: N(X) depends only on floor(X), and Y = X L^(-c_1) <= X / 200^(c_1) for X >= 2^200: at eta -> 0, 200^(1/h*) = 264.4, so floor(Y) < floor(X) and the induction on floor(X) is well-founded;
       the note says 'strong induction' over real X without this remark: a presentational gap, not an error.
   size of X_3 (2 L^(-eta) + L^(-a) <= 1): log_2 log_2 X_3 for a = 0.02, 0.05, 0.1:
      a=0.020 eta=0.00155: log_2 L >= 650.5, i.e. X_3 ~ 2^(2^650)
      a=0.050 eta=0.00905: log_2 L >= 114.0, i.e. X_3 ~ 2^(2^114)
      a=0.100 eta=0.02155: log_2 L >= 48.9, i.e. X_3 ~ 2^(2^49)
   (vii) Corollary 4: the recursion in 1.7 is N_A(X) <= k N_A(X^(1-theta)) + #F_b + #F_(-b) + (k+1)(|b|/3+1) with base N_A <= 2X: (R) with a doubled no-dip term and an extra O(k) term, so 27 -> 54 and K adjusts; the polylog argument transfers, but '(R) verbatim' is not literally accurate.

